IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nrsr-dates`
IMPORT `nrsr-survivor`

-- Cases for the survivor's seat of the National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text before the run. Day counts were counted on a calendar:
-- 15 November 2027 to 15 September 2027 is -61 days (15 + 31 + 15 back); to 15 December 2027 is 30 days; 1 June 2027 to
-- 15 September 2027 is 106 days (30 + 31 + 31 + 14).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

GIVEN d IS A DEONTIC `Rules party` `Rules step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ends fulfilled` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`on` d m y MEANS `the calendar day` d m y

§ `The dates`

#ASSERT `the sunset day of the scheme` EQUALS `on` 1 7 2028
#ASSERT `the eighteenth birthday for` (`on` 15 3 2010) EQUALS `on` 15 3 2028
-- Born 29 February 2008: no 29 February in 2026, so 18 on 1 March 2026 (fork F3).
#ASSERT `the eighteenth birthday for` (`on` 29 2 2008) EQUALS `on` 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `the matching day` (0 MINUS 4) `months from` (`on` 31 7 2027) EQUALS `on` 31 3 2027
-- February 2027 has no 31st or 30th: the last day of February.
#ASSERT `the matching day` (0 MINUS 3) `months from` (`on` 31 5 2027) EQUALS `on` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the days from` (`on` 15 11 2027) `until` (`on` 15 9 2027) EQUALS (0 MINUS 61)
#ASSERT `the days from` (`on` 15 11 2027) `until` (`on` 15 12 2027) EQUALS 30

§ `Rules s 4B -- eligible as a child migrant`

-- The base case: arrived 1950 aged 9 from the United Kingdom, sent by a charity under an Empire Settlement Act scheme,
-- no adult family here, made a ward of a participating State, abused in a home while a ward.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible as a child migrant question` 1950 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I am eligible for redress as a child migrant from the United Kingdom or Malta (Rules s 4B; Act s 13(2)); Australian citizenship or permanent residence (Act s 13(1)(e)) is not one of its conditions`
-- "before 1984": 1983 is in, 1984 is out.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible as a child migrant question` 1983 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I am eligible for redress as a child migrant from the United Kingdom or Malta (Rules s 4B; Act s 13(2)); Australian citizenship or permanent residence (Act s 13(1)(e)) is not one of its conditions`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible as a child migrant question` 1984 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no, not under Rules s 4B(2)(a): I did not arrive before 1984 as a child sent from the United Kingdom or Malta by an institution, with no family in Australia except children`
-- An adult member of the family was already here.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible as a child migrant question` 1950 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no, not under Rules s 4B(2)(a): I did not arrive before 1984 as a child sent from the United Kingdom or Malta by an institution, with no family in Australia except children`
-- Arrived as an adult.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible as a child migrant question` 1950 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no, not under Rules s 4B(2)(a): I did not arrive before 1984 as a child sent from the United Kingdom or Malta by an institution, with no family in Australia except children`
-- Neither route in (2)(b); then the guardianship route alone.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible as a child migrant question` 1950 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no, not under Rules s 4B(2)(b): I was not sent under an Empire Settlement Act 1922 scheme, nor made a ward under the National Security (Overseas Children) Regulations or the Immigration (Guardianship of Children) Act 1946`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible as a child migrant question` 1950 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I am eligible for redress as a child migrant from the United Kingdom or Malta (Rules s 4B; Act s 13(2)); Australian citizenship or permanent residence (Act s 13(1)(e)) is not one of its conditions`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible as a child migrant question` 1950 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no, not under Rules s 4B(2)(c)-(d): I did not become a ward of a participating State or Territory, or the abuse did not occur while I was its ward`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible as a child migrant question` 1950 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no, not under Rules s 4B(2)(c)-(d): I did not become a ward of a participating State or Territory, or the abuse did not occur while I was its ward`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible as a child migrant question` 1950 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no, not under Rules s 4B(1)(a)-(d): the sexual abuse is not within the scope of the scheme, would attract no redress payment under the assessment framework, or no participating or listed institution is responsible for it`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible as a child migrant question` 1950 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no, not under Rules s 4B(1)(a)-(d): the sexual abuse is not within the scope of the scheme, would attract no redress payment under the assessment framework, or no participating or listed institution is responsible for it`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible as a child migrant question` 1950 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no, not under Rules s 4B(1)(a)-(d): the sexual abuse is not within the scope of the scheme, would attract no redress payment under the assessment framework, or no participating or listed institution is responsible for it`

§ `Rules s 6 -- abuse by another child`

#ASSERT `Does abuse by another child count question` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `out of the scope: sexual abuse by another child that involved neither physical contact with me nor penetration of me is not within the scope of the scheme (Rules s 6)`
#ASSERT `Does abuse by another child count question` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Rules s 6 does not take it out: the abuse involved physical contact or penetration; whether it is within the scope is decided by Act s 14`
#ASSERT `Does abuse by another child count question` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 6 does not take it out: the abuser was not a child; whether it is within the scope is decided by Act s 14`
#ASSERT `Does abuse by another child count question` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 6 does not take it out: it speaks only of sexual abuse; whether non-sexual abuse is within the scope is decided by Act s 14`

§ `Rules s 8 -- the government that placed me`

-- A State welfare department, a participating institution, placed a ward of the State in a church orphanage.
#ASSERT `Is the government that placed me equally responsible question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the participating government institution is equally responsible with the non-government institution that cared for me, and the non-government institution is not primarily responsible (Rules s 8(1), (6); Act s 15(5), (6))`
#ASSERT `Is the government that placed me equally responsible question` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the participating government institution is equally responsible with the non-government institution that cared for me, and the non-government institution is not primarily responsible (Rules s 8(1), (6); Act s 15(5), (6))`
-- Neither a court order for parental responsibility nor a ward (s 8(3) fails).
#ASSERT `Is the government that placed me equally responsible question` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 8 does not make them equally responsible: not every circumstance in Rules s 8(2)-(5) existed; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
-- Others outside the s 8(4) list also had parental responsibility.
#ASSERT `Is the government that placed me equally responsible question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 8 does not make them equally responsible: not every circumstance in Rules s 8(2)-(5) existed; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
-- Abused while in the care of another institution too (s 8(5) fails).
#ASSERT `Is the government that placed me equally responsible question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 8 does not make them equally responsible: not every circumstance in Rules s 8(2)-(5) existed; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
-- s 11(4) item 1: a court ordered the government institution to pay, and s 8(2)-(4) are met.
#ASSERT `Is the government that placed me equally responsible question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Rules s 8 does not apply: a court has ordered the government institution to pay me compensation or damages for the abuse, so it is not responsible at all (Rules s 11(2), (4) item 1)`
-- A court order, but no arrangement: item 1 does not reach it, and s 8 does not make it equally responsible.
#ASSERT `Is the government that placed me equally responsible question` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Rules s 8 does not make them equally responsible: not every circumstance in Rules s 8(2)-(5) existed; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
#ASSERT `Is the government that placed me equally responsible question` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 8 does not apply: the government institution is not a participating institution`

§ `Rules s 9 -- cadets`

-- "on or after 1 January 1977": the first day is in, the day before is out.
#ASSERT `Is Defence equally responsible for abuse in cadets question` (`on` 1 1 1977) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a Commonwealth institution that deals with defence is equally responsible with each institution otherwise responsible for the abuse, and none of them is primarily responsible (Rules s 9(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Is Defence equally responsible for abuse in cadets question` (`on` 31 12 1976) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 9 does not apply: the abuse occurred before 1 January 1977 (Rules s 9(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is Defence equally responsible for abuse in cadets question` (`on` 5 5 1985) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 9 does not apply: the conditions in Rules s 9(1)(b)-(d) are not all met; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
#ASSERT `Is Defence equally responsible for abuse in cadets question` (`on` 5 5 1985) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 9 does not apply: the conditions in Rules s 9(1)(b)-(d) are not all met; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
#ASSERT `Is Defence equally responsible for abuse in cadets question` (`on` 5 5 1985) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 9 does not apply: the conditions in Rules s 9(1)(b)-(d) are not all met; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
#ASSERT `Is Defence equally responsible for abuse in cadets question` (`on` 5 5 1985) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Rules s 9 does not apply: a court has ordered the Commonwealth defence institution to pay me compensation or damages for the abuse, so it is not responsible at all (Rules s 11(2), (4) item 2)`

§ `Rules s 10 -- child migrants`

#ASSERT `Who is responsible for abuse of a child migrant question` 1950 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `all equally responsible: the Commonwealth Department administering the Immigration (Guardianship of Children) Act 1946, the State or Territory institution that had me as its ward, and each other institution otherwise responsible (Rules s 10(2)); no institution is responsible except under s 10(2) (s 10(3))`
#ASSERT `Who is responsible for abuse of a child migrant question` 1950 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the same, except the institution a court ordered to pay me: it is not responsible, and Rules s 10 does not apply (Rules s 11(2), (4) item 3); responsibility is decided under Act s 15 and Rules s 11`
#ASSERT `Who is responsible for abuse of a child migrant question` 1984 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 10 does not apply: I am not a child migrant covered by Rules s 10(1); responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
#ASSERT `Who is responsible for abuse of a child migrant question` 1950 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 10 does not apply: I am not a child migrant covered by Rules s 10(1); responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
#ASSERT `Who is responsible for abuse of a child migrant question` 1950 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 10 does not apply: I am not a child migrant covered by Rules s 10(1); responsibility is decided under Act s 15`

§ `Rules s 11 -- an institution ordered by a court to pay me`

#ASSERT `Is an institution ordered by a court to pay me still responsible question` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not responsible: the institution ordered to pay me is not responsible for the abuse under the scheme (Rules s 11(2)); other institutions may still be responsible`
#ASSERT `Is an institution ordered by a court to pay me still responsible question` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not responsible: the institution ordered to pay me is not responsible for the abuse under the scheme (Rules s 11(2)); and no other institution is responsible for it either (s 11(3))`
#ASSERT `Is an institution ordered by a court to pay me still responsible question` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not responsible: the institution ordered to pay me is not responsible for the abuse under the scheme (Rules s 11(2)); other institutions may still be responsible`
#ASSERT `Is an institution ordered by a court to pay me still responsible question` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 11 does not apply: the order was a consent order (Rules s 11(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is an institution ordered by a court to pay me still responsible question` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 11 does not apply: the order was set aside on appeal (Rules s 11(1)(b))`
-- A class action judgment: the group member who opted out of the share keeps the institution in the scheme.
#ASSERT `Is an institution ordered by a court to pay me still responsible question` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 11 does not apply: the order was for a group payment and I chose not to accept my share (Rules s 11(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `Is an institution ordered by a court to pay me still responsible question` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not responsible: the institution ordered to pay me is not responsible for the abuse under the scheme (Rules s 11(2)); other institutions may still be responsible`
-- (1)(c) speaks only of a group order: "choosing not to accept" an order to me alone changes nothing.
#ASSERT `Is an institution ordered by a court to pay me still responsible question` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not responsible: the institution ordered to pay me is not responsible for the abuse under the scheme (Rules s 11(2)); other institutions may still be responsible`
#ASSERT `Is an institution ordered by a court to pay me still responsible question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 11 does not apply: no court has ordered the institution to pay me compensation or damages for the abuse`
#ASSERT `Rules s 11(1) -- a court order for compensation or damages applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Rules s 11(1) -- a court order for compensation or damages applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))

§ `Rules s 12 -- a government body that only regulated or funded`

#ASSERT `Is a government body that only regulated or funded responsible question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not responsible: the government authority's only connection with the abuse is that it regulated, funded or established the other institution (Rules s 12(2))`
#ASSERT `Is a government body that only regulated or funded responsible question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not responsible: the government authority's only connection with the abuse is that it regulated, funded or established the other institution (Rules s 12(2))`
#ASSERT `Is a government body that only regulated or funded responsible question` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not responsible: the government authority's only connection with the abuse is that it regulated, funded or established the other institution (Rules s 12(2))`
#ASSERT `Is a government body that only regulated or funded responsible question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 12 does not apply: the authority had some other connection with the abuse; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
#ASSERT `Is a government body that only regulated or funded responsible question` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 12 does not apply: the authority had some other connection with the abuse; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
#ASSERT `Is a government body that only regulated or funded responsible question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Rules s 12 gives way: the authority is responsible under Rules Part 3 Division 2 (ss 8-10), which s 12 is subject to (s 12(3))`
#ASSERT `Is a government body that only regulated or funded responsible question` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 12 does not apply: the institution is not an authority of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory`
#ASSERT `Is a government body that only regulated or funded responsible question` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 12 does not apply: the abuse was not in another institution's care, by its official, or on its premises or in its activities (Rules s 12(1))`

§ `Rules s 15 -- applying as a child`

-- Born 15 March 2010: 18 on 15 March 2028, before the sunset day. Applied 15 November 2027, exactly 4 months before.
#ASSERT `When will my application as a child be decided question` (`on` 15 11 2027) (`on` 15 3 2010) EQUALS `the Operator must give me a notice in this window, and cannot decide before I turn 18 on this day; then it must decide as soon as practicable (Rules s 15(2)-(4))` (`on` 15 9 2027) (`on` 15 12 2027) (`on` 15 3 2028)
-- One day later: less than 4 months before.
#ASSERT `When will my application as a child be decided question` (`on` 16 11 2027) (`on` 15 3 2010) EQUALS `no notice is required because I applied less than 4 months before turning 18; the Operator cannot decide before I turn 18 on this day, then must decide as soon as practicable (Rules s 15(2)-(4))` (`on` 15 3 2028)
-- Applied on the 18th birthday: no longer a child.
#ASSERT `When will my application as a child be decided question` (`on` 15 3 2028) (`on` 15 3 2010) EQUALS `Rules s 15 does not apply: I was not a child on the day I applied`
#ASSERT `When will my application as a child be decided question` (`on` 14 3 2028) (`on` 15 3 2010) EQUALS `no notice is required because I applied less than 4 months before turning 18; the Operator cannot decide before I turn 18 on this day, then must decide as soon as practicable (Rules s 15(2)-(4))` (`on` 15 3 2028)
-- Born 1 July 2010: 18 on the sunset day itself, not before it.
#ASSERT `When will my application as a child be decided question` (`on` 1 1 2026) (`on` 1 7 2010) EQUALS `Rules s 15 does not apply: I will not turn 18 before the scheme sunset day (1 July 2028); Act s 20(1)(c) bars the application`
-- Born 30 June 2010: 18 on 30 June 2028. 4 months before is 29 February 2028 (no 30th in February 2028); the window runs
-- from 30 December 2027 to 30 March 2028.
#ASSERT `When will my application as a child be decided question` (`on` 1 1 2028) (`on` 30 6 2010) EQUALS `the Operator must give me a notice in this window, and cannot decide before I turn 18 on this day; then it must decide as soon as practicable (Rules s 15(2)-(4))` (`on` 30 12 2027) (`on` 30 3 2028) (`on` 30 6 2028)
#ASSERT `When will my application as a child be decided question` (`on` 1 3 2028) (`on` 30 6 2010) EQUALS `no notice is required because I applied less than 4 months before turning 18; the Operator cannot decide before I turn 18 on this day, then must decide as soon as practicable (Rules s 15(2)-(4))` (`on` 30 6 2028)
#ASSERT `When will my application as a child be decided question` (`on` 29 2 2028) (`on` 30 6 2010) EQUALS `the Operator must give me a notice in this window, and cannot decide before I turn 18 on this day; then it must decide as soon as practicable (Rules s 15(2)-(4))` (`on` 30 12 2027) (`on` 30 3 2028) (`on` 30 6 2028)

-- The notice, applied 15 November 2027, born 15 March 2010: window days -61 to 30.
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice about turning 18 in time question` (`on` 15 11 2027) (`on` 15 3 2010) TRUE (`on` 15 12 2027) (`on` 1 1 2028) EQUALS `given in time (Rules s 15(2))`
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice about turning 18 in time question` (`on` 15 11 2027) (`on` 15 3 2010) TRUE (`on` 20 11 2027) (`on` 1 1 2028) EQUALS `given in time (Rules s 15(2))`
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice about turning 18 in time question` (`on` 15 11 2027) (`on` 15 3 2010) TRUE (`on` 16 12 2027) (`on` 1 1 2028) EQUALS `late: the Operator did not give me the notice by 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2)); it still must not decide before I turn 18 (s 15(3))`
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice about turning 18 in time question` (`on` 15 11 2027) (`on` 15 3 2010) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 15 12 2027) EQUALS `not yet due: the Operator has until 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2))`
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice about turning 18 in time question` (`on` 15 11 2027) (`on` 15 3 2010) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 16 12 2027) EQUALS `late: the Operator did not give me the notice by 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2)); it still must not decide before I turn 18 (s 15(3))`
-- Applied 1 June 2027: the window opens on day 106 (15 September 2027); a notice on 14 September is too early.
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice about turning 18 in time question` (`on` 1 6 2027) (`on` 15 3 2010) TRUE (`on` 14 9 2027) (`on` 1 10 2027) EQUALS `given too early: more than 6 months before I turn 18, so it is not the notice Rules s 15(2) requires; that notice is still owed`
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice about turning 18 in time question` (`on` 1 6 2027) (`on` 15 3 2010) TRUE (`on` 15 9 2027) (`on` 1 10 2027) EQUALS `given in time (Rules s 15(2))`
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice about turning 18 in time question` (`on` 16 11 2027) (`on` 15 3 2010) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 1 3 2028) EQUALS `no notice is required (Rules s 15(2) does not apply to my application)`
-- The rule itself.
#ASSERT `ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`Rules s 15(2) -- the Operator must give me a notice 3 to 6 months before I turn 18` (0 MINUS 61) 30) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Operator` (`give me the notice about turning 18` 30) 30)))
#ASSERT `ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`Rules s 15(2) -- the Operator must give me a notice 3 to 6 months before I turn 18` (0 MINUS 61) 30) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Operator` (`give me the notice about turning 18` 0) 0)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`Rules s 15(2) -- the Operator must give me a notice 3 to 6 months before I turn 18` (0 MINUS 61) 30) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 31), (EVENT `the Operator` (`give me the notice about turning 18` 31) 31)))))
#ASSERT (NOT (`ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`Rules s 15(2) -- the Operator must give me a notice 3 to 6 months before I turn 18` 106 197) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Operator` (`give me the notice about turning 18` 105) 105)))))
-- expect: BREACH BY the Operator (no notice by day 30)
#TRACE `Rules s 15(2) -- the Operator must give me a notice 3 to 6 months before I turn 18` (0 MINUS 61) 30 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)

§ `Rules s 17 -- revoking the decision`

#ASSERT `Can the decision on my application be revoked question` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `cannot be revoked: I have accepted the offer of redress (Act s 29(5))`
#ASSERT `Can the decision on my application be revoked question` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `must be revoked: I notified the Operator that I accepted an offer of payment relating to the abuse (Rules s 17(3)(a), s 74)`
#ASSERT `Can the decision on my application be revoked question` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `must be revoked: the Operator has learned for the first time of a payment to me under a court order for the abuse (Rules s 17(3)(b), (4)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can the decision on my application be revoked question` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `must be revoked: the Operator has learned for the first time of a payment to me by or for a responsible institution for the abuse (Rules s 17(3)(b), (4)(b))`
-- A payment wholly excluded by s 26 (say, workers' compensation): no duty; with information that would change the decision, a power.
#ASSERT `Can the decision on my application be revoked question` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 17 gives the Operator no ground to revoke on these facts`
#ASSERT `Can the decision on my application be revoked question` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `may be revoked: the Operator has received information it did not have that would have changed the determination (Rules s 17(2))`
#ASSERT `Can the decision on my application be revoked question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `may be revoked: the Operator has received information it did not have that would have changed the determination (Rules s 17(2))`
#ASSERT `Can the decision on my application be revoked question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 17 gives the Operator no ground to revoke on these facts`

§ `Rules s 26 -- earlier payments`

-- A $50,000 settlement from the responsible church body, all for the abuse.
#ASSERT `How much of an earlier payment counts against my redress question` TRUE `any other payment (for example a settlement, an ex gratia payment or a payment under an institution's own scheme)` 50000 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 50000
-- $10,000 of it for something else, $5,000 for counselling costs: 35,000 counts.
#ASSERT `How much of an earlier payment counts against my redress question` TRUE `any other payment (for example a settlement, an ex gratia payment or a payment under an institution's own scheme)` 50000 10000 5000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 35000
-- The parts not counted exceed the payment: nothing counts.
#ASSERT `How much of an earlier payment counts against my redress question` TRUE `any other payment (for example a settlement, an ex gratia payment or a payment under an institution's own scheme)` 50000 30000 30000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much of an earlier payment counts against my redress question` TRUE `any other payment (for example a settlement, an ex gratia payment or a payment under an institution's own scheme)` 50000 0 50000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much of an earlier payment counts against my redress question` TRUE `compensation under the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988` 50000 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much of an earlier payment counts against my redress question` TRUE `a payment under Chapter 3, 4, 5, 5A, 6 or 11 of the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004` 50000 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much of an earlier payment counts against my redress question` TRUE `a payment under a Part of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 listed in Rules s 26(3)(d)` 50000 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much of an earlier payment counts against my redress question` TRUE `any other payment (for example a settlement, an ex gratia payment or a payment under an institution's own scheme)` 50000 0 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
-- Paid for several institutions together: the s 26(6) formula is lost from the deposit.
#ASSERT `How much of an earlier payment counts against my redress question` TRUE `any other payment (for example a settlement, an ex gratia payment or a payment under an institution's own scheme)` 50000 0 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 26(2): the subsections do not limit one another; a listed payment is out wholly even if made for several.
#ASSERT `How much of an earlier payment counts against my redress question` TRUE `compensation under the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988` 50000 0 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much of an earlier payment counts against my redress question` FALSE `any other payment (for example a settlement, an ex gratia payment or a payment under an institution's own scheme)` 50000 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0

§ `Rules s 31 -- the acceptance document`

#ASSERT `Does my acceptance document have what the Rules require question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `complete: it has each responsible institution's share of the costs, the earlier payments and their effect, and my consent for released institutions and officials (Rules s 31)`
#ASSERT `Does my acceptance document have what the Rules require question` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `complete: it has each responsible institution's share of the costs, the earlier payments and their effect, and my consent for released institutions and officials (Rules s 31)`
#ASSERT `Does my acceptance document have what the Rules require question` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `missing: the amount of each responsible institution's share of the costs of the redress payment (Rules s 31(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Does my acceptance document have what the Rules require question` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `missing: the amount of an earlier payment from a responsible institution, or a statement of its effect on that institution's share (Rules s 31(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Does my acceptance document have what the Rules require question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `missing: my consent to released institutions and officials using and disclosing my protected information in the document to obtain the benefit of Act s 43 (Rules s 31(3))`

§ `Rules s 33 -- where the payment goes`

#ASSERT `Where will my redress payment be paid question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `into an account I hold with a financial institution and have nominated in writing to the Operator (Rules s 33(2))`
#ASSERT `Where will my redress payment be paid question` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `into an account the administrator appointed for my affairs holds with a financial institution and has nominated in writing (Rules s 33(4); Act s 48(1A))`
#ASSERT `Where will my redress payment be paid question` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `into an account with a financial institution nominated in writing by the executor or administrator of my estate (Rules s 33(3))`
-- Died, but the nominated account is still open: s 33(3)(c) is not met.
#ASSERT `Where will my redress payment be paid question` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `into an account I hold with a financial institution and have nominated in writing to the Operator (Rules s 33(2))`
-- Both (3) and (4) could apply: (3) taken (fork F5).
#ASSERT `Where will my redress payment be paid question` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `into an account with a financial institution nominated in writing by the executor or administrator of my estate (Rules s 33(3))`
#ASSERT `Where will my redress payment be paid question` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `already paid into my nominated account; Rules s 33 asks for nothing more`

§ `Rules ss 34-35C -- notices when the applicant dies`

#ASSERT `What notice follows the applicant's death question` `before the Operator decided the application (Act s 58)` EQUALS `a written notice to the person the Operator considers most appropriate (not an institution): whether the application was approved, the reasons, and if approved the amount of the redress payment (Rules s 34)`
#ASSERT `What notice follows the applicant's death question` `after an offer of redress, before it was accepted, declined or withdrawn, with no review pending (Act s 59(3))` EQUALS `a written notice to each person the Operator decides should be paid the redress payment, stating the amount to be paid to that person (Rules s 35(2); Act s 60)`
#ASSERT `What notice follows the applicant's death question` `after an offer of redress, while a review of the decision was pending (Act s 59(4))` EQUALS `a written notice of the outcome of the review to the person or persons the Operator considers most appropriate: the outcome (including whether the payment is payable under Act s 60 and to whom) and the reasons (Rules s 35(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `What notice follows the applicant's death question` `during a reassessment, after applying for review of the reassessment decision (Act s 71M(4))` EQUALS `a written notice of the reassessment decision to the person the Operator considers most appropriate: the reasons for the review of the reassessment decision, the total redress payable, and any increase over the current determination (Rules s 35A)`
#ASSERT `What notice follows the applicant's death question` `during a reassessment, before the reassessment decision (Act s 71N(3))` EQUALS `a written notice of the reassessment decision to each person the Operator considers most appropriate: the reasons, the total redress payable, and any increase over the current determination (Rules s 35B)`
#ASSERT `What notice follows the applicant's death question` `before the current determination was identified for reassessment (Act s 71P(3))` EQUALS `a written notice of the reassessment decision to the person the Operator considers most appropriate: the reasons, the total redress payable, and any increase over the current determination (Rules s 35C)`
#ASSERT `What notice follows the applicant's death question` `after accepting the offer of redress` EQUALS `none under Rules Part 8 Division 3: the offer was accepted, so the redress is paid under Rules s 33`

§ `Rules s 37 -- the special assessment decision`

#ASSERT `Will I be told the special assessment decision question` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Operator must give me written notice of its decision, and also each institution it asked for information about my application (Rules s 37(2))`
#ASSERT `Will I be told the special assessment decision question` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Operator must give me written notice of its decision (Rules s 37(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Will I be told the special assessment decision question` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Operator must give me written notice of its decision (Rules s 37(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Will I be told the special assessment decision question` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Rules s 37 does not apply: the Operator has decided that I am not prevented from being entitled to redress`
#ASSERT `Will I be told the special assessment decision question` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Rules s 37 does not apply: neither a sentence for an offence in Act s 63(2)(a) nor a special assessment determination`

§ `Rules s 39 -- security notices`

#ASSERT `What does a security notice do to my application question` `I had applied, and no decision or no offer had yet been made` EQUALS `my application is taken to be withdrawn (Act s 71(1)); the Operator must give me written notice of the withdrawal (Rules s 39(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `What does a security notice do to my application question` `I had an offer of redress not yet accepted, declined or withdrawn` EQUALS `my offer is taken to be withdrawn, the decision revoked and my application withdrawn (Act s 71(2)); the Operator must give written notice of all three to me and to each institution and person it had notified of the decision or offer, unless that institution gets notice of the withdrawal under Act s 23 (Rules s 39(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `What does a security notice do to my application question` `I had agreed to a reassessment, and no reassessment decision had been made` EQUALS `I am taken to have revoked my agreement to the reassessment (Act s 71(2A)); Rules s 39 applies, but s 39(2) names no notice of a revoked agreement`
#ASSERT `What does a security notice do to my application question` `I had agreed to a reassessment, and had a new offer not yet accepted, declined or withdrawn` EQUALS `my new offer is taken to be withdrawn, the reassessment decision revoked and my agreement to the reassessment revoked (Act s 71(2B)); Rules s 39(2)(b)(iii)-(iv) point to notices to those told of the reassessment, but s 39(2) names no notice of these three effects`
#ASSERT `What does a security notice do to my application question` `I had already accepted or declined my offer` EQUALS `Rules s 39 does not apply: Act s 71 does not reach an offer already accepted or declined`

§ `Rules Part 11 -- public interest disclosure`

#ASSERT `Can my information be disclosed in the public interest question` `protecting the public revenue (Rules s 44)` `someone with a genuine and legitimate interest in the information connected with that purpose` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `may be certified: the Operator may certify the disclosure necessary in the public interest, if it is satisfied of these matters, having had regard to the impact the disclosure might have on me (Rules ss 42, 43(1); Act s 95(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can my information be disclosed in the public interest question` `protecting the public revenue (Rules s 44)` `someone with a genuine and legitimate interest in the information connected with that purpose` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no, not under Rules s 43: the information can reasonably be obtained from a source other than the Department and Services Australia (s 43(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can my information be disclosed in the public interest question` `some other purpose` `a Minister listed in Rules s 43(2)` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no, not under Rules s 43: the disclosure is not covered by any of Rules ss 44 to 54A (s 43(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can my information be disclosed in the public interest question` `a proceeds of crime or unexplained wealth order, disclosed to a law enforcement agency (Rules s 46)` `someone with a genuine and legitimate interest in the information connected with that purpose` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no, not under Rules s 43: the disclosure is not to the kind of recipient, or not in the circumstances, that the section for its purpose names`
#ASSERT `Can my information be disclosed in the public interest question` `locating a missing person, disclosed to a court, coroner, Royal Commission or government authority (Rules s 51)` `someone with a genuine and legitimate interest in the information connected with that purpose` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no, not under Rules s 43: there is reasonable ground to believe the person the information is about would not want it disclosed (Rules s 51(c), s 52(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `Can my information be disclosed in the public interest question` `matters about a deceased person (Rules s 52(1))` `a Minister listed in Rules s 43(2)` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `may be certified: the Operator may certify the disclosure necessary in the public interest, if it is satisfied of these matters, having had regard to the impact the disclosure might have on me (Rules ss 42, 43(1); Act s 95(1)(a))`
-- The "would not want it" condition belongs to ss 51 and 52(1) only.
#ASSERT `Can my information be disclosed in the public interest question` `research, statistics or policy on institutional child sexual abuse (Rules s 53)` `someone with a genuine and legitimate interest in the information connected with that purpose` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `may be certified: the Operator may certify the disclosure necessary in the public interest, if it is satisfied of these matters, having had regard to the impact the disclosure might have on me (Rules ss 42, 43(1); Act s 95(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can my information be disclosed in the public interest question` `aged care means testing (Rules s 54A)` `someone else` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no, not under Rules s 43: the recipient has no genuine and legitimate interest connected with the purpose and is not a listed Minister (s 43(1)(c))`

§ `Rules s 71 -- my settlement deed`

#ASSERT `Can my settlement deed stop me using the scheme question` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the term does not have that effect, and is not enforceable so far as it would have it (Rules s 71(2))`
-- A confidentiality clause alone.
#ASSERT `Can my settlement deed stop me using the scheme question` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the term does not have that effect, and is not enforceable so far as it would have it (Rules s 71(2))`
#ASSERT `Can my settlement deed stop me using the scheme question` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the term does not have that effect, and is not enforceable so far as it would have it (Rules s 71(2))`
#ASSERT `Can my settlement deed stop me using the scheme question` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 71 does not apply: the term would not prevent or limit my applying for or receiving redress, the institution's liability or payment under the scheme, or disclosure in connection with the scheme`
#ASSERT `Can my settlement deed stop me using the scheme question` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Rules s 71 does not apply: the term is not in an agreement or deed under which I released a participating or listed institution from liability for abuse within the scope of the scheme`

§ `Rules s 72 -- a prison sentence`

#ASSERT `Must I tell the Operator about my prison sentence question` TRUE 5 TRUE EQUALS `yes: I must notify the Operator in writing, in the approved form, as soon as practicable after I know of the sentence (Act s 181(1); Rules s 72)`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Operator about my prison sentence question` TRUE 4.99 TRUE EQUALS `no, not under Act s 181(1): the sentence is less than 5 years`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Operator about my prison sentence question` TRUE 8 FALSE EQUALS `no, not under Act s 181(1): I was sentenced before I applied (Act s 63 still applies to that sentence)`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Operator about my prison sentence question` FALSE 8 TRUE EQUALS `no, not under Act s 181(1): I have not applied for redress`

§ `Rules ss 73-74 -- a payment offer I accepted`

#ASSERT `Must I tell the Operator about a payment offer I accepted question` `after I applied, before I was given notice of the Operator's determination` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I must notify the Operator in writing as soon as practicable, naming the institution by or for which the payment is to be paid (Rules s 73(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Operator about a payment offer I accepted question` `after I applied, before I was given notice of the Operator's determination` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no, not under Rules ss 73-74: the payment is not from or for an institution those sections name, or does not relate to the abuse`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Operator about a payment offer I accepted question` `after I applied, before I was given notice of the Operator's determination` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no, not under Rules ss 73-74: the payment is not from or for an institution those sections name, or does not relate to the abuse`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Operator about a payment offer I accepted question` `after I was given notice approving my application, before I accepted or declined the offer of redress` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I must notify the Operator in writing as soon as practicable and in any case before I accept the offer of redress, naming the institution by or for which the payment is to be paid (Rules s 74(2), (3)); the Operator must then revoke its determination (Rules s 17(3)(a))`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Operator about a payment offer I accepted question` `after I was given notice approving my application, before I accepted or declined the offer of redress` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no longer: I have declined the offer of redress, so Rules s 74(2) and (3) have ceased to apply (s 74(4))`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Operator about a payment offer I accepted question` `after I was given notice approving my application, before I accepted or declined the offer of redress` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no, not under Rules ss 73-74: the payment is not from or for an institution those sections name, or does not relate to the abuse`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Operator about a payment offer I accepted question` `before I applied for redress` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no, not under Rules ss 73-74: I did not accept the payment offer in the period those sections cover`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Operator about a payment offer I accepted question` `after I was given notice that my application was not approved` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no, not under Rules ss 73-74: I did not accept the payment offer in the period those sections cover`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Operator about a payment offer I accepted question` `after I accepted the offer of redress` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no, not under Rules ss 73-74: I did not accept the payment offer in the period those sections cover`

-- Payment offer accepted 1 March 2026; offer of redress accepted 10 March 2026 (day 9).
#ASSERT `Did I tell the Operator about the payment in time question` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 5 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `in time: I notified the Operator before accepting my offer of redress (Rules s 74(2)); whether it was as soon as practicable is not decided here`
-- Same day (fork F6).
#ASSERT `Did I tell the Operator about the payment in time question` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `in time: I notified the Operator before accepting my offer of redress (Rules s 74(2)); whether it was as soon as practicable is not decided here`
#ASSERT `Did I tell the Operator about the payment in time question` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 11 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `late: I accepted my offer of redress before notifying the Operator (Rules s 74(2))`
#ASSERT `Did I tell the Operator about the payment in time question` (`on` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `late: I accepted my offer of redress before notifying the Operator (Rules s 74(2))`
#ASSERT `Did I tell the Operator about the payment in time question` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 5 3 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `done: I notified the Operator, and have not yet accepted my offer of redress (Rules s 74(2)); whether it was as soon as practicable is not decided here`
#ASSERT `Did I tell the Operator about the payment in time question` (`on` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `still due: I must notify the Operator as soon as practicable, and before I accept my offer of redress (Rules s 74(2))`
